# size 12x3
# Growing, after the old size forced content to scroll.
#
# Five lines on a three-row screen: two are in the scrollback before the resize happens. That is
# what makes this case able to tell a resize applied at the right moment from one applied before
# the writes that precede it - with the resize first, nothing ever scrolls and there is no history
# at all. A case that cannot tell those apart is not testing the ordering it claims to.
\e[H\e[2Jone\r\ntwo\r\nthree\r\nfour\r\nfive
# resize 24x6
\e[6;1H012345678901234567890123
